Confluent 8.2.1 Version
======================

>> add the below entries in server.properties 

##################### Confluent Metrics Reporter #######################

metric.reporters=io.confluent.metrics.reporter.ConfluentMetricsReporter 
confluent.metrics.reporter.bootstrap.servers=localhost:9092
confluent.metrics.reporter.topic.replicas=1
confluent.metrics.reporter.security.protocol=PLAINTEXT


>> Add the below entries in /etc/profile
export CONFLUENT_HOME=/home/ubuntu/Desktop/kafka/confluent-8.2.1
export CONFLUENT_CURRENT="/home/ubuntu/Desktop/kafka/logs"
export CONTROL_CENTER_HOME=/home/ubuntu/Desktop/kafka/softwares/confluent-control-center-next-gen-2.3.0


1. Start the internal Prometheus engine
./prometheus-start

2. Route Alertmanager cleanly to port 9098
export ALERTMANAGER_PORT=9098
./alertmanager-start

3. Start the confluent platform
./confluent local services start

4. prometheus console
http://localhost:9090

5. Confluent control center 
http://localhost:9021

#############################################################################################################
Telemetry Reporter to view broker metrics (Confluent Cloud)

> add the below properties in server.properties

confluent.telemetry.enabled=true
confluent.telemetry.api.key=<CLOUD_API_KEY>
confluent.telemetry.api.secret=<CLOUD_API_SECRET>

We need a Confluent Cloud account and a Cloud API Key. Confluent documentation explicitly states that telemetry 
reporting (Health+/cloud telemetry) requires a Confluent Cloud API key and secret.
